@id("close-workorder-main-with-recent-human-approval")
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"MaintData___close_workorder", resource)
when { context.input.site_id == "MAIN" }
when temporal {
  formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Dorvane___get_approval"::response{
    eventResource: resource,
    input.site_id: context.input.site_id,
    input.wonum: context.input.wonum,
    output.decision: "GRANTED",
    output.approver_kind: "HUMAN"
  }
};

// The approval lookup must itself be permitted, or its response is never recorded.
// The other read-only lookups are permitted here as well.
@id("read-only-lookups")
permit (
  principal,
  action in [
    Drupe::Action::"Dorvane___get_approval",
    Drupe::Action::"Kelvora___get_approval",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_failure_codes",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_my_assigned_workorders",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_schedule_calendar",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_actuals_vs_planned",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_costs",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_kpis",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___get_workorder_tasks",
    Drupe::Action::"MaintData___list_workorders"
  ],
  resource
);

@id("agent-never-approves")
forbid (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"MaintData___approve_workorder", resource);
```

Closing is permitted only at MAIN, and only after a completed `Dorvane___get_approval` call earlier in the session. That call must have been for the same `wonum` and `site_id`, within the last hour. Its output must show `decision` GRANTED and `approver_kind` HUMAN. A rejected, pending, agent-made or system-made approval does not match.

I did not use `Kelvora___get_approval` as proof of approval. Its `decision` and `approver_kind` fields are plain strings with no documented values. Treating it as proof would mean guessing literals, and a wrong guess could let an unverified approval through. It can still be called as a read-only lookup. If you confirm what values it returns, I can add it as a second source.

`MaintData___approve_workorder` is explicitly forbidden, and nothing else is permitted. The other tools, such as assign, update, cancel and generate, are denied by default.

